The texts of the licenses are in LICENSE. Each Go file says where it comes from.

What was left out: every interface, event and method that the driver does not call (about 230 files of
the original became 60), the fixed-version runtime and the other options of the loader, and the
GUID code adapted from go-ole (windows.GUIDFromString does its job).

What was changed, because the original does the wrong thing for what the driver calls (the original is
generated code that Wails itself does not use for these calls; see the comment of package webview2):

  - the methods that return a string through an out parameter (get_Source, get_Uri, get_DocumentTitle...)
    passed a null pointer where the address of the pointer is due;
  - ICoreWebView2Settings3..6 were looked up on the web view, not on its settings;
  - ICoreWebView2Environment.CreateCoreWebView2Controller passed the address of the HWND, not the HWND;
  - put_Bounds passed the RECT by address on every architecture (wrong on arm64);
  - an HRESULT is read as 32 bits;
  - three conversions from an integer to a pointer that go vet refuses.

The code has been compiled for windows/amd64 and windows/arm64 and never run on Windows at the time of
writing: see the matrix of manual tests (docs/qa/m18-webview-matrice.md, section Windows).
